    },
    "schema:description": "Metadata harvested directly from NCEI NOAA landing page JSON-LD by Claude Code. Converted to CDIF discovery profile: Property names prefixed with schema: namespace; Unprefixed properties assigned to unk: namespace (contentURL); @context set to CDIF prefix declarations (extra prefixes preserved); @type values normalized to arrays with schema: prefix; @id set from schema:url; Distributions normalized; schema:creator wrapped in @list; Agent objects fixed (Person name synthesis, sameAs arrays). Distribution schema:url mapped to schema:contentUrl; GeoShape box array converted to string. Note added 2026-10-09: the source is the schema.org JSON-LD embedded in the NCEI landing page https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/access/metadata/landing-page/bin/iso?id=gov.noaa.nodc:GHRSST-MUR-JPL-L4-GLOB , which this record's schema:url redirects to. That JSON-LD lists 7,588 schema:hasPart accessions; for this example the list is truncated to the first 100. Each part carried only an alternateName and a url, so to meet CDIF core: schema:name was copied from its alternateName; @id and schema:identifier were set from its url; schema:dateModified was set to 1900-01-01, a sentinel meaning not recorded; schema:conditionsOfAccess was copied from this collection; and schema:subjectOf points to this catalog record. The root is typed schema:Collection as well as schema:Dataset, since it is a series of accessions. Each accession has a full record of its own -- name, dates, creator, distribution, and isPartOf back to this collection -- in the application/ld+json of its landing page, e.g. https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/access/metadata/landing-page/bin/iso?id=gov.noaa.nodc:0078754 , which would be a better source for the parts."
  },
